    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97134.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "Well, there really are no circumstances that an election wouldn't take place. And it's going to be really interesting because even though one minute he thinks he controls everything and then he doesn't control, I mean, he's a mess. But really, the only folks that could change the election would be the governors. But by the Constitution, the Constitution says we have to vote for a president on the first Tuesday in November. But the interesting thing is, is that let's just say whatever and it didn't happen. He has to leave on January 20th. Him and his buddy have to leave. And if they don't leave and get evicted, then Speaker Pelosi becomes the president.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
