    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97134.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 103,
    "turn_text": "But this is what's frustrating to me. I mean, the house has done its job. I think one, I think one, we're all learning a lot more about government than we did before because we see where, like you said, this example, it can be broken or it cannot fully function and we understand the balance of government. But this is the first time that I've seen a situation where, okay, the train is off the tracks. The house is doing their job, but we know no matter how much you do your job, you still have to have the Senate to come and do their job.",
